  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The brasserie</h2>
      <p>Chez Mô is at 46 boulevard Albert 1er, on the corner by the seafront, a short walk from the ramparts of Antibes according to its website. It is a large seafood and Mediterranean brasserie with its own fishmonger, a sushi counter and takeaway dishes. The dining rooms are bright, with large windows and some tables near the aquariums, and the terrace looks out to sea. The restaurant is air-conditioned.</p>
      <p>The summer 2026 menu highlights seafood platters (from the Écailler at €31 to a platter for two at €92), oysters, live shellfish, grilled fish, lobster, seafood paella and choucroute, as well as homemade sushi. The website advertises a "Chez Mô" menu at €32 excluding drinks or €41 with drinks, and two weekday lunch set menus at €20.90 (not weekends or public holidays), with a drink and a coffee. Cheques are no longer accepted.</p>

      <h2>Dogs at the table</h2>
      <p>The Antibes Juan-les-Pins tourist office, Destination Côte d'Azur France and Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourism all list "Animals accepted" among the restaurant's services, next to the terrace, air conditioning, baby chair and wifi. The restaurant's website does not mention animals, and none of these listings says whether dogs may come inside or only sit on the terrace.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book mentioning that you are coming with your dog, and ask for a terrace table. The restaurant can be reached every day from 9:30am to 8pm on 04 93 34 33 54 (except Sunday at lunchtime).</div>

      <h2>Hours and access</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is open 7 days a week without a break, from 12pm to 10pm (10:30pm in summer, last order). The fishmonger next door is open from 12pm to 8pm. Bookings made less than two days ahead, for more than six people or for takeaway are handled by phone.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The ramparts of the old town of Antibes are close by and the seafront is right in front of the terrace: a chance to walk your dog on a leash before or after the meal.</p>
